    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose elite score of 83.29 makes him the clear centerpiece of the lineup. Facing a favorable matchup against Bibee, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an excellent park factor (+16%) and a slow opposing delivery that significantly enhances his stolen base upside, a critical component of our strategy. Joining him as a high-efficiency play is **Jackson Merrill** (75.10), who draws a soft matchup against Cornelio (5.59 xERA). The combination of a high-value lineup spot and the weakest opposing arm on the slate allows **Jackson Merrill** to provide the core production we need to maintain our lead in the category races.\n\nThe primary lineup construction decision focused on the utility spot, where **Coby Mayo** (61.85) edged out **Tommy White** (52.17). While **Tommy White** remains a solid bench option with decent park factors against Jos\u00e9 Soriano, **Coby Mayo** is elevated by his favorable park context and the sheer volume of high-leverage opportunities batting fourth. We are currently monitoring **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose 66.54 score assumes he retains the #3 spot; should his position shift downward upon the final release of the lineup, his efficiency score may require a minor re-calibration. Meanwhile, **Luis Lara** remains our most volatile start at 48.58, though his ability to contribute across multiple facets keeps him ahead of the remaining bench depth.\n\nWe are navigating the stretch run with a thin bench due to the prolonged absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg**, all of whom remain on the IL. This lack of depth places a premium on our daily efficiency scores for starters like **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin**, both of whom are projected near the 60 threshold. While **Sam Antonacci** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** provide strong stability at the top and middle of the order respectively, the team must remain vigilant regarding weather shifts and late-scratches. With SB remaining our scarcest category, every stolen base attempt from **Gunnar Henderson** and **Henry Bolte** is being calculated as a high-value outcome to keep the Austin Waves ahead of the pack.",
